  "hook": "My family's Puerto Rican restaurant in Brooklyn had survived forty-seven years, three landlords, two hurricanes, and Covid. It could not survive the new property tax assessment. I needed five hundred thousand dollars in forty-five days. Alistair Warrington-Blake, the British CEO of a hedge fund whose lease was up on his visa, offered the amount in exchange for a three-year marriage. I said yes with olive oil on my fingers and my mother's spoon in my back pocket. We were married on Saturday. The ICE officer came to our apartment three weeks later.",
